# ultranix-mcp - uinput access for the evdev input fallback.
#
# OPT-IN: this rule is inert until the dedicated `ultranix-input` group
# exists and the single service user is added to it - group membership is
# the opt-in gate. Setup: packaging/README-uinput.md (installed at
# /usr/share/doc/ultranix-mcp/README-uinput.md).
#
# NEVER GROUP="input" - `input` membership grants read of *real* input
# devices, i.e. a keylogger permission (docs/THREAT_MODEL.md §4.1).
# Add ONLY the service user to `ultranix-input`; nothing else belongs there.
SUBSYSTEM=="uinput", MODE="0660", GROUP="ultranix-input", OPTIONS+="static_node=uinput"
